00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.830 align:start position:0%
 
this morning on the dish  our visit to a remote island off the  coast of maine for a clambake  put on by even tide one of the most  successful seafood restaurants in the  country  the team who started even thai just  released their first cookbook called  eventide a tribute to friendship fishing  and classic seafood dishes pushed to the  edge  of perfection  our journey began by boats in casco bay  off the coast of freeport maine our  guides  james beard award winning chef andrew  taylor and his business partner arlen  smith  the destination little whale boat island  welcome good to be here once ashore the  ingredients for our feast were brought  in  and the wood was kindled quinn big is  going to happen yeah baby  waiting in the wings a smorgasbord of  delights from the waters of casco bay  oh there we go yeah you want help with  that yes sir  [Applause]  all of it layered with freshly gathered  seaweed for true ocean flavor  a tradition pioneered by native  americans  as the fire warmed taylor had time to  forage for extras  across this 22-acre island on a  picture-perfect day  a skill he's honed over a lifetime of  living the new england lifestyle  this is what i really was going for for  the uh you know the mignonette this is  called c-rocket  these are c-rocket pods the culinary  experience the eventside founders were  creating for us here is something  they've been trying to do in one way or  another for diners  in maine for the past eight years it's  like a fine dining aesthetic in a  casual place yeah yeah we we wanted to  keep the atmosphere completely casual we  wanted it to feel almost like a bar  really  but at the same time serve really kind  of like elegant and interesting food  portland maine has become a culinary hub  in recent years  and making a mark is not easy even tide  has excelled by putting a unique twist  on the classic sea shack one of the  things you talk about a lot in the book  is the fact that some of these  shacks in other places have been around  for generations and yet you were  surprised at the lack of sort of  creativity  or change that's come about in some of  these dishes  it's not even something i necessarily  think is a negative you know  people people love the standbys i mean  people come to maine for a classic  lobster roll or a boiled lobster and  and there are plenty of places to do  that and we just wanted to do something  a little bit different with those places  as sort of like our baseline  but we came out with more of a culinary  sensibility that includes their  signature  a lobster roll with brown butter served  on a chinese style bun one of the best  lunch plates we've ever had  a wide variety of succulent main oysters  and fresh local tuna sliced thin and  served crudo style  on the day we visited even during a  pandemic there was a  three-hour wait for lunch by  mid-afternoon  why does a place like even ty do you  think just take off from the beginning  i do think that event in particular gave  people something that they wanted when  they came to maine  and you guys had like a 20 or 30 year  plan when you first opened right like  there was an effect there was a detailed  exact outlook on what was yeah  yeah we didn't know what we were doing  and uh it was a it was a total fiasco  to be perfectly honest um we  grossly miscalculated how busy we would  be how much did it did it surprised you  that it was such a hit  i think quite a bit i mean it truly  honestly surprised  us um but but maine can be a struggle  maine can be difficult  oh it smells good back on little whale  boat island  on the morning of the clambake the pot  was getting closer  you'll start to see some steam coming  from the top and once the steam starts  it's usually around  15 minutes 10 15 minutes there is the  intimidation factor about clam bakes  people think they're complicated like  that's  you can make that somebody can make that  you make that right at home right in  your stove at home  or outside in your fire pit or put it on  your grill outside  taylor stacked up a gorgeous display  choose your own adventure here that's  what i love about it  don't mind if i do and  the big boy hello  lobster corn knock wurst eggs  steamers and mussels with steam buns  all served with butter and a nuri  mignonette for dipping  delicious well the mini nuts is  fantastic yeah it's really good right  oh my gosh yes  to finish it off an even tied specialty  the e t and g our house tonic is made  with uh cinchona bark and a bunch of  other herbs and spices this already has  the gin in it  you said in the book there might be  nothing better than this to drink with  oysters  nope why i think partially  for me it just just feels like summer  so we do that and then uh just soda  water and a lime of course  cheers cheers it's a little whale boat  and great food and drink  and friends indeed  it's yummy it was yummy and our sincere  thanks to the maine coast heritage trust  for helping to facilitate that trip  and also helping to protect some of  these islands over the years  which makes this possible and people  able to get there beautiful  food beautiful setting michelle has a  question for you  i'll make a handbag for you i'm happy to  i don't eat clams or lobsters that's  that's the only reason you're up there  well there's other good stuff though  there  yeah the corn the potatoes and the point  is that the  clambake is as he said in the piece it's  not that difficult to make just look  that was good that was great all around

